(3359213, 458680, 60354, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jasonlprice:</b></div><hr/><i> One negative for me is that it seems like the left books are softer focus than the right?  That is probably just an optical illusion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, I''d say i should have chosen a different aisle and cared more about the balance of the shot.  The books on the left are no less in focus than the ones on the right, but their dimmer contrast and less vivid colors make you think otherwise.  Anyway, I''m just a beginner, but will try better.</td>', 'Originally posted by jasonlprice: One negative for me is that it seems like the left books are softer focus than the right?  That is probably just an optical illusion.   Yes, I''d say i should have chosen a different aisle and cared more about the balance of the shot.  The books on the left are no less in focus than the ones on the right, but their dimmer contrast and less vivid colors make you think otherwise.  Anyway, I''m just a beginner, but will try better.', '2007-02-12 22:26:53.000000', NULL, 0),
